reg_canon: cs-programming; vocabulary := exact identifiers (rsync, --delete, --dry-run, systemctl --user, HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC/DST/LOG, cp -a, systemd unit directives).
A1_src: HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC default := /opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/ (canonical host-side mount, kb digests)
A1_dst: HERMES_CONTEXT_DST default := /workspace/hermes-context/ (exists; holds INDEX.md, agents/, config/)
A2_direction: ∀ run -> sync host->workspace, one-way; ¬∃ writeback to SRC
A3_standalone: script must execute without systemd; units are systemctl --user, no root
A4_fallback: ¬∃ rsync -> cp -a semantics (or tar pipe); semantics: contents of SRC/ -> DST (trailing-slash mirror), never DST/SRC-nest
A5_mirror: ∀ run -> DST end state == SRC end state exactly; rsync path uses --delete; cp fallback reconciles (no accumulate-only); both paths converge to identical end state
A6_dryrun_purity: --dry-run -> ZERO writes ∀ targets, incl. log files; DST byte-identical post-dry-run (mechanical gate: full-tree byte compare, not probe-file)
A7_recursive: A5 is recursive; cp fallback deletes stale subtrees ∀ depth (mirrors rsync --delete); README sync-strategy section states this
A8_placement: log path := ~/.cache/hermes-context/ default, ALWAYS outside DST (∀ modes, no carve-outs, no post-mirror rewrite); install paths := ~/.local/bin (or /workspace/hdcs/bin), never artifact/ inside DST; sync never deletes/moves its own entrypoints
invariants:
  I1: ∀ mode m ∈ {real, dry} -> DST_post(dry) == DST_pre
  I2: ∀ real run -> DST_post == SRC (recursive, byte-faithful)
  I3: ∀ artifact (log, script, unit, README) -> artifact ∉ mirrored tree
  I4: idempotent: run^2 == run^1
open: none — all ambiguities resolved by A1..A8
